1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,465
GTA 6 doesn't explain half of its best

2
00:00:02,465 --> 00:00:04,931
systems. Some of them you'll only discover twenty

3
00:00:04,931 --> 00:00:07,396
hours in. So here are twenty-five tips I

4
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:09,862
wish I'd known on day one, starting with

5
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:12,327
the basics and ending with the ones that

6
00:00:12,327 --> 00:00:13,560
change how you play.

7
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:15,927
Some of these will save you hours, a

8
00:00:15,927 --> 00:00:18,045
couple will save you a lot of money,

9
00:00:18,045 --> 00:00:20,162
and one of them is permanent, so you'll

10
00:00:20,162 --> 00:00:22,279
want to know about it before you make

11
00:00:22,279 --> 00:00:23,338
your first big mistake.

12
00:00:23,588 --> 00:00:26,206
Tip one: Focus Mode. Click both sticks at

13
00:00:26,206 --> 00:00:28,823
once. Outside of combat you can hold it

14
00:00:28,823 --> 00:00:31,441
as long as you like, and with a

15
00:00:31,441 --> 00:00:33,404
gun out it briefly slows time.

16
00:00:33,654 --> 00:00:36,562
Focus colour-codes the world. Enemies show up red,

17
00:00:36,562 --> 00:00:39,470
things you can interact with show yellow, and

18
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:42,378
cash shows green. You can spot enemies through

19
00:00:42,378 --> 00:00:45,286
walls, follow animal tracks, check car trunks for

20
00:00:45,286 --> 00:00:48,194
valuables, and find notes with safe codes on

21
00:00:48,194 --> 00:00:48,558
them.

22
00:00:48,808 --> 00:00:51,502
Tip two: doors talk to you. In Focus,

23
00:00:51,502 --> 00:00:54,197
a white door means you can go in.

24
00:00:54,197 --> 00:00:56,891
A red door means it's alarmed. Check before

25
00:00:56,891 --> 00:00:58,912
you open anything during a job.

26
00:00:59,162 --> 00:01:01,903
Tip three: find the hidden rooms. Inside any

27
00:01:01,903 --> 00:01:04,645
shop, walk toward the back and watch the

28
00:01:04,645 --> 00:01:07,386
minimap. If it shows a back room, a

29
00:01:07,386 --> 00:01:10,127
staircase, or a door that won't open, there's

30
00:01:10,127 --> 00:01:11,498
more to that building.

31
00:01:11,748 --> 00:01:14,767
Tip four: read the map colours. Dark blue

32
00:01:14,767 --> 00:01:17,786
buildings have an entrance or interior. Light blue

33
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,805
buildings are just scenery. That alone saves you

34
00:01:20,805 --> 00:01:22,692
a lot of pointless walking.

35
00:01:22,942 --> 00:01:25,676
And when you're near an enterable building, the

36
00:01:25,676 --> 00:01:28,411
minimap marks the entrance, usually with a small

37
00:01:28,411 --> 00:01:31,145
white line. Rockstar packed this world with interiors,

38
00:01:31,145 --> 00:01:32,854
so it pays to look.

39
00:01:33,104 --> 00:01:36,018
Tip five: your character has three core stats.

40
00:01:36,018 --> 00:01:38,933
Health is your life bar, Stamina is for

41
00:01:38,933 --> 00:01:41,847
sprinting and exertion, and Focus decides how long

42
00:01:41,847 --> 00:01:43,304
you can slow time.

43
00:01:43,554 --> 00:01:47,556
Each one trains differently. Lifting weights raises Health.

44
00:01:47,556 --> 00:01:51,559
Cardio, like running, biking or kayaking, raises Stamina.

45
00:01:51,559 --> 00:01:55,561
And calm activities, like fishing or playing pool,

46
00:01:55,561 --> 00:01:56,562
raise Focus.

47
00:01:56,812 --> 00:01:59,692
Tip six, and this is a big one:

48
00:01:59,692 --> 00:02:02,572
Focus gains are permanent. Health and Stamina fade

49
00:02:02,572 --> 00:02:05,452
if you stop training, but Focus stays. So

50
00:02:05,452 --> 00:02:08,332
go fishing early. It's the best long-term upgrade

51
00:02:08,332 --> 00:02:09,412
in the game.

52
00:02:09,662 --> 00:02:12,794
Tip seven: buffs. Food, sleep and showers give

53
00:02:12,794 --> 00:02:15,925
temporary boosts, marked by a pink heart for

54
00:02:15,925 --> 00:02:19,057
Health, a blue lightning bolt for Stamina, and

55
00:02:19,057 --> 00:02:21,014
a purple eye for Focus.

56
00:02:21,264 --> 00:02:24,459
A simple daily routine works: sleep at night,

57
00:02:24,459 --> 00:02:27,655
work out in the morning, eat, then shower.

58
00:02:27,655 --> 00:02:30,850
And feed Dolores, Jason's pet snake, for a

59
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:32,448
small early Focus boost.

60
00:02:32,698 --> 00:02:35,603
Tip eight: the fitness app. Stop training once

61
00:02:35,603 --> 00:02:38,508
your ring closes, then have a protein bar

62
00:02:38,508 --> 00:02:41,412
or shake. The window reopens every in-game day,

63
00:02:41,412 --> 00:02:43,954
so training past it is wasted time.

64
00:02:44,204 --> 00:02:47,049
Tip nine: train together. If both characters work

65
00:02:47,049 --> 00:02:49,894
out at the gym, both of them benefit,

66
00:02:49,894 --> 00:02:52,028
no matter which one you're controlling.

67
00:02:52,278 --> 00:02:55,603
Tip ten: there's no fast travel by map.

68
00:02:55,603 --> 00:02:58,929
No tapping a marker and warping. Your options

69
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:02,254
are the RydeMe app, public transport, or switching

70
00:03:02,254 --> 00:03:02,670
characters.

71
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:05,350
With RydeMe you mark a spot and call

72
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,780
a car. Pay an extra hundred dollars and

73
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:10,209
you arrive instantly. That's the closest thing to

74
00:03:10,209 --> 00:03:11,728
fast travel in the game.

75
00:03:11,978 --> 00:03:14,887
Buses and trains run on schedules, and the

76
00:03:14,887 --> 00:03:17,796
trains cover the whole region. And the fastest,

77
00:03:17,796 --> 00:03:20,705
cheapest option of all is switching characters, because

78
00:03:20,705 --> 00:03:23,614
the other one usually waits near your current

79
00:03:23,614 --> 00:03:23,978
safehouse.

80
00:03:24,228 --> 00:03:27,153
Tip eleven: do the Keys side content early.

81
00:03:27,153 --> 00:03:30,078
Treasure diving, fishing, and your neighbour Shirley's requests

82
00:03:30,078 --> 00:03:33,002
are all down there, and coming back later

83
00:03:33,002 --> 00:03:35,196
takes around ten minutes each way.

84
00:03:35,446 --> 00:03:38,118
While you're down there, explore the main strip.

85
00:03:38,118 --> 00:03:40,790
Bars like the Rusty Anchor and the Cheeky

86
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:43,462
Mutineer are full interiors, and Key Lento is

87
00:03:43,462 --> 00:03:46,134
a great place to learn the controls before

88
00:03:46,134 --> 00:03:47,470
the city gets busy.

89
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,382
Tip twelve: time matters. Press up on the

90
00:03:50,382 --> 00:03:53,044
d-pad to check it on your phone. Some

91
00:03:53,044 --> 00:03:55,706
shops close at night, some missions only run

92
00:03:55,706 --> 00:03:58,368
at certain times, and you can skip time

93
00:03:58,368 --> 00:04:00,032
by sleeping at Jason's house.

94
00:04:00,282 --> 00:04:02,910
Tip thirteen: your cash isn't safe in your

95
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:05,537
pocket. Before you get a bank account, hide

96
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:08,165
it under the loose floorboards in Jason's bedroom.

97
00:04:08,165 --> 00:04:10,793
You'll even find old photos there that fill

98
00:04:10,793 --> 00:04:11,778
in his backstory.

99
00:04:12,028 --> 00:04:14,541
Your first bank account comes in the mission

100
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:17,055
Buck Me, roughly one to two hours in.

101
00:04:17,055 --> 00:04:19,568
After that, deposit after every big job, because

102
00:04:19,568 --> 00:04:22,082
if you die you lose the cash you're

103
00:04:22,082 --> 00:04:22,396
carrying.

104
00:04:22,646 --> 00:04:25,590
Tip fourteen: don't grind for money early. Spend

105
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:28,534
on things that actually help, like weapons and

106
00:04:28,534 --> 00:04:31,478
vehicle mods, and let the story open up

107
00:04:31,478 --> 00:04:32,582
the bigger earners.

108
00:04:32,832 --> 00:04:35,942
Tip fifteen: buy a suppressor. There's an Ammu-Nation

109
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:39,053
in Key Lento right after the tutorial, suppressors

110
00:04:39,053 --> 00:04:42,163
are cheap, and they reduce the police response

111
00:04:42,163 --> 00:04:44,496
to gunshots, which buys you time.

112
00:04:44,746 --> 00:04:47,408
Tip sixteen: get a red dot sight. It

113
00:04:47,408 --> 00:04:50,070
lets you click the right stick to aim

114
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:52,066
in first person. Iron sights don't.

115
00:04:52,316 --> 00:04:55,655
Tip seventeen: scout first. The map shows each

116
00:04:55,655 --> 00:04:58,993
robbery's potential take and its security level before

117
00:04:58,993 --> 00:04:59,828
you commit.

118
00:05:00,078 --> 00:05:02,892
Low security jobs, which is every shop in

119
00:05:02,892 --> 00:05:05,706
the starting area except the bank, need one

120
00:05:05,706 --> 00:05:08,521
person. Medium and high security are much easier

121
00:05:08,521 --> 00:05:11,335
as a duo, so invite your partner from

122
00:05:11,335 --> 00:05:12,390
the map icon.

123
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:15,283
Tip eighteen: use the back door. The snap

124
00:05:15,283 --> 00:05:17,926
gun gets you in without setting off the

125
00:05:17,926 --> 00:05:20,568
alarm. And safe codes are randomised, so look

126
00:05:20,568 --> 00:05:23,211
for them with Focus instead of trusting an

127
00:05:23,211 --> 00:05:23,872
old guide.

128
00:05:24,122 --> 00:05:26,797
Tip nineteen: you can pass stash bags to

129
00:05:26,797 --> 00:05:29,472
your partner. Press right on the d-pad, then

130
00:05:29,472 --> 00:05:32,148
circle or B. Your partner sells the loot

131
00:05:32,148 --> 00:05:34,154
while you deal with the police.

132
00:05:34,404 --> 00:05:36,679
And whatever you do, don't die with a

133
00:05:36,679 --> 00:05:38,954
full bag. If you go down, you lose

134
00:05:38,954 --> 00:05:41,229
the cash and the stash bags you were

135
00:05:41,229 --> 00:05:43,504
carrying, so the escape is part of the

136
00:05:43,504 --> 00:05:43,788
job.

137
00:05:44,038 --> 00:05:46,790
Tip twenty: avoid banks and loan stores early.

138
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:49,542
Their cash has dye packs, and you need

139
00:05:49,542 --> 00:05:52,294
a dye pack jammer from Chapter 3 before

140
00:05:52,294 --> 00:05:53,326
they're worth robbing.

141
00:05:53,576 --> 00:05:56,330
One more robbery detail: a store you've robbed

142
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:59,084
closes for a while afterwards. So you can't

143
00:05:59,084 --> 00:06:01,839
farm the same shop over and over. Spread

144
00:06:01,839 --> 00:06:03,560
your jobs around the map.

145
00:06:03,810 --> 00:06:06,898
Tip twenty-one: the police track what they know

146
00:06:06,898 --> 00:06:09,986
about you. Your face, your outfit, your car,

147
00:06:09,986 --> 00:06:13,074
your weapon, CCTV footage, and whether Jason and

148
00:06:13,074 --> 00:06:16,162
Lucia were together. Each one shows as an

149
00:06:16,162 --> 00:06:17,706
icon under your stars.

150
00:06:17,956 --> 00:06:20,737
And each one has its own fix. A

151
00:06:20,737 --> 00:06:23,519
hat or mask for your face, a full

152
00:06:23,519 --> 00:06:26,300
outfit change for your clothes, a different car,

153
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:29,081
putting your gun away, destroying the CCTV footage,

154
00:06:29,081 --> 00:06:30,124
and splitting up.

155
00:06:30,374 --> 00:06:33,056
Tip twenty-two: your car's trunk is a lifesaver.

156
00:06:33,056 --> 00:06:35,738
Your personal vehicle keeps spare outfits in it,

157
00:06:35,738 --> 00:06:38,421
and weapons you drop go back to your

158
00:06:38,421 --> 00:06:41,103
trunk. Call your car and change on the

159
00:06:41,103 --> 00:06:41,438
spot.

160
00:06:41,688 --> 00:06:44,612
Tip twenty-three: night can be safer for jobs,

161
00:06:44,612 --> 00:06:47,535
because the police react differently after dark. Plan

162
00:06:47,535 --> 00:06:49,728
your bigger scores for the evening.

163
00:06:49,978 --> 00:06:52,735
And if the stars climb to three or

164
00:06:52,735 --> 00:06:55,491
more, a normal car struggles to escape. A

165
00:06:55,491 --> 00:06:58,248
fast motorbike, or ducking through alleys on foot,

166
00:06:58,248 --> 00:07:01,004
works much better. The police try non-lethal takedowns

167
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,761
first, but they will kill you if you

168
00:07:03,761 --> 00:07:04,450
fight back.

169
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:07,622
Tip twenty-four is the permanent one: your criminal

170
00:07:07,622 --> 00:07:10,544
profile. Jason and Lucia each have one, and

171
00:07:10,544 --> 00:07:13,466
it tracks how you commit crimes over time.

172
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:16,388
It isn't a simple good or evil scale.

173
00:07:16,638 --> 00:07:20,634
There are five levels: Professional, Hardened, Violent, Psycho,

174
00:07:20,634 --> 00:07:24,631
and Irredeemable. Professional means low violence and non-lethal

175
00:07:24,631 --> 00:07:28,627
takedowns, and you even fill Focus by being

176
00:07:28,627 --> 00:07:30,126
kind to citizens.

177
00:07:30,376 --> 00:07:33,479
At Psycho you can't surrender to the police.

178
00:07:33,479 --> 00:07:36,582
And Irredeemable is permanent. A ruthless profile also

179
00:07:36,582 --> 00:07:39,685
means faster police calls, armed citizens and more

180
00:07:39,685 --> 00:07:42,789
aggressive responses. So decide early what kind of

181
00:07:42,789 --> 00:07:44,728
criminal you want to be.

182
00:07:44,978 --> 00:07:47,919
It even affects your partner. The character you

183
00:07:47,919 --> 00:07:50,859
aren't controlling behaves according to their own profile.

184
00:07:50,859 --> 00:07:53,800
And remember, head and heart shots kill, while

185
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:56,741
limbs and joints only injure. Red hit markers

186
00:07:56,741 --> 00:07:58,946
mean a kill, yellow means injured.

187
00:07:59,196 --> 00:08:02,291
Tip twenty-five, a non-lethal trick for chases: shoot

188
00:08:02,291 --> 00:08:05,386
out one or two tyres and pursuing cars

189
00:08:05,386 --> 00:08:08,481
spin out. Helicopters back off after enough shots

190
00:08:08,481 --> 00:08:08,868
too.

191
00:08:09,118 --> 00:08:11,800
One last chase tip: the minimap doesn't show

192
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:14,483
the police or their vision cones anymore. Open

193
00:08:14,483 --> 00:08:17,165
the full map during a search to see

194
00:08:17,165 --> 00:08:19,847
the red zone, and use Focus to reveal

195
00:08:19,847 --> 00:08:20,518
nearby officers.

196
00:08:20,768 --> 00:08:23,476
Two bonus tips. Before you steal a car,

197
00:08:23,476 --> 00:08:26,184
scan it with the Waink app on your

198
00:08:26,184 --> 00:08:28,892
phone. It shows the security system, the sell

199
00:08:28,892 --> 00:08:30,584
price and the registration cost.

200
00:08:30,834 --> 00:08:33,511
And plan for a garage. You can only

201
00:08:33,511 --> 00:08:36,187
buy them after Jason and Lucia leave Key

202
00:08:36,187 --> 00:08:38,864
Lento, but they store vehicles for free, hold

203
00:08:38,864 --> 00:08:41,541
your weapon loadout, and let you drop off

204
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:42,210
illegal goods.

205
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,788
Quick recap of the big ones. Use Focus

206
00:08:45,788 --> 00:08:49,116
Mode everywhere. Fish early, because Focus is permanent.

207
00:08:49,116 --> 00:08:52,444
Bank your cash. Scout robberies and bring your

208
00:08:52,444 --> 00:08:55,772
partner. Fix every heat icon. And watch your

209
00:08:55,772 --> 00:08:58,684
criminal profile, because Irredeemable never goes away.

210
00:08:58,934 --> 00:09:01,748
Which tip surprised you most? Tell me in

211
00:09:01,748 --> 00:09:04,561
the comments. And subscribe, because next we're touring

212
00:09:04,561 --> 00:09:07,375
every region of Leonida and what's waiting in

213
00:09:07,375 --> 00:09:08,078
each one.
